      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1885 the newly renamed Burke boasted three sawmills, three cotton gins, a church and a school, signaling rapid early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://burketexas.com/history/burke.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Burke was established before the nearby cities of Lufkin and Diboll, which did not yet exist when the town was founded.",
